  "aiContextParagraph": "Cyclone Akvan has moved toward India's eastern coast, prompting extensive disaster management responses across Odisha, Andhra Pradesh, and parts of Jharkhand. Government officials in Odisha ordered the evacuation of roughly 300,000 people to safer zones as part of emergency preparations, while high-level coordination meetings were held to oversee crisis management. In Srikakulam district of Andhra Pradesh, heavy precipitation has already caused flooding in low-lying areas like Ichchapuram and Sompeta, with record rainfall levels reported. Rail networks across the affected states are experiencing widespread service interruptions, with numerous trains being redirected or halted to ensure safety. Regional authorities remain on high alert, with schools in some districts suspending primary classes and emergency teams deployed to conduct rescue and relief operations as the storm continues its path.",
